  m_Name: Note_Audio_OceansResponse1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NoteData
  title: The Water Secrets
  key: 19
  topic: 1
  boardContentText: 'The ocean reacts to changes in the lighthouse signal


    Something
    beneath the water appears to be responding


    There is strange movement observed
    beneath the water'
  boardSprite: {fileID: 0}
  contentText: 'EMIL: My audio diary. Next entry.

    [pause]

    EMIL: Something
    is happening here. And it isn''t just in my head. ...At least, that''s what I
    keep telling myself.

    [brief silence]

    EMIL: I''ve been standing by the
    tower. For hours. Watching the sea.

    [pause]

    EMIL: When I tried switching
    the lighthouse around again... something stirred in the water. Not waves. Something
    deeper. Something big. Beneath the surface.

    [longer silence]

    EMIL:
    And then again. And again.

    [pause]

    EMIL: Every time I change the beam,
    something moves down there. Every time.

    [hesitation]

    EMIL: That''s
    not normal. ...Someone would have seen this by now.

    [brief silence]

    EMIL:
    Unless I''m the only one even looking.

    [longer pause, waves]

    EMIL:
    ...And there''s something else. Something I can''t put together.

    [silence]

    EMIL:
    It''s like I can hear Marie. My wife. ...Like I can see her. Down there, beneath
    the water.

    [brief silence]

    EMIL: Marie''s been dead a long time. She''s
    gone. I know that. I buried... no, I didn''t even bury her. I wasn''t there.

    [pause]

    EMIL:
    And now I feel her here. I see her.

    [longer silence]

    EMIL: ...Have
    I lost my mind?

    [click]'
  paperSprite: {fileID: 0}
